@startuml resolve-and-reopen
title US-13: Resolution and Later Recurrence - New Episode Creates New Alert

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

actor Operator
participant "Express API" as API
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts table" as TSDB
participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka

== Operator Resolves Alert ==

Operator -> API : PATCH /alerts/VesselB:SIGNAL_LOSS:1700000000000\n{ status: RESOLVED }
API -> TSDB : UPDATE alert to RESOLVED\nrecord resolved_at / resolved_by
TSDB --> API : updated
API --> Operator : 200 OK

note over TSDB
  Resolved record remains permanent history.
  RESOLVED is terminal.
end note

== Same anomaly occurs in a later episode ==

note over Evaluator
  VesselB later goes dark again.
  New dark_since_ms means a different
  deterministic signal-loss identity.
end note

Evaluator -> Kafka : publish SIGNAL_LOSS\nalert_id = VesselB:SIGNAL_LOSS:1700005000000
Kafka -> API : consume new alert
API -> TSDB : INSERT new alert row\nstatus = NEW\nON CONFLICT DO NOTHING

note over TSDB
  Two independent records exist:
  old episode -> RESOLVED
  new episode -> NEW

  There is no reopen operation.
end note

@enduml
